# Static first hyperpolarizability of LiH -- the smallest `quadratic` deck.
# One direction (z, the molecular axis), one rung (protocol 1e-4, k 6): alpha_zz(0)
# and beta_zzz(0;0,0). LiH is polar, so beta_zzz is large (~3e2 au) and a
# meaningful regression number; a centrosymmetric molecule would give zero.
# `l 50.0` rather than 80.0 to hold the wall down: the larger box costs 8 s and
# moves beta_zzz by 0.08 % (315.512 -> 315.777).
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=response response_lih_beta.in)

dft
    xc        hf
    dconv     1e-4
    k         6
    protocol  [1e-4]
    l         50.0
    localize  new
    maxiter   30
end

response
    dipole              true
    dipole.directions   z
    dipole.frequencies  [0.0]
    quadratic           true
    kain                true
    dconv               1e-4
    maxiter             60
    print_level         1
end

molecule
    eprec      1e-6
    no_orient  true
    units      angstrom
    Li  0.0  0.0  -0.803105264950
    H   0.0  0.0   0.803105264950
end
